.TH CALEN 1.SH NAMEcalen \- a month as a diary page.SH SYNOPSIS\fBcalen\fR[\-b\fIn\fR] [\-l|\-r] [\-m|\-u] [\-o\fIseq\fR].SH DESCRIPTION\fBcalen\fRprints a month as a page for a diary, ruled into days for appointments,with the month's name in large letters and the months before and afteras small calendars in the corners.  It reads the month, the year and howmany months to print from its standard input:.nf    echo 9 2026 1 | calen > september.fiFor a printer, each page ends with a form feed..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-b\fIn\fR\fIn\fRblank lines after each form feed..TP 12\fB\-l, \-r\fRdates left-justified (the default) or right-justified..TP 12\fB\-m, \-u\fRmixed case (the default) or upper case..TP 12\fB\-o\fIseq\fRuse\fIseq\fRas the overstrike sequence for bold..SH SEE ALSOcal, calender